Juan River\nBasin, Southwest San Juan Mountains and Uncompahgre Plateau and\nDallas Divide and southeast Utah, including the following areas,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through late Wednesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will be possible over burn scars, at low-water\ncrossings, and along creeks, streams, washes, arroyos and other\nflood-prone locations. Creeks and streams may rise out of their\nbanks. Unpaved roads could become muddy and impassable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Periods of heavy rainfall, associated with remnant moisture from\nHurricane Polo, are expected to produce numerous showers and\nembedded thunderstorms. Heavy rain falling on saturated soils and\nburn scars could lead to localized flash flooding and rises on\nlocal rivers. Rainfall is expected to end by late Wednesday, but\nrivers may rise out of their banks overnight Wednesday even after\nrainfall has ended.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-01T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0131f538810dac521ad09e37656bcfc83b15cbff.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0131f538810dac521ad09e37656bcfc83b15cbff.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-30T19:12:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 301912 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 112 PM MDT Wed Sep 30 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Widespread rainfall continues through the evening across southeast Utah and southwest Colorado. Isolated storms cannot be ruled out. - Flooding concerns continue over the rain-soaked terrain, especially within and adjacent to the southern San Juans. A Floo","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-30T19:20:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION